WEBVTT

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:26.620
What was the sea monster that attacked and mauled this American warship?

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.140
Did a giant octopus, as big as Piccadilly Circus, come ashore on this beach?

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:43.380
Did the legendary serpent of the sea appear to this Cornish fisherman?

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:47.830
Out come the head, about three feet away from the body, had a good look at it,

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:52.180
presumably didn't like to look away, and he just disappeared, smurged.

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:56.510
Mysteries from the files of Arthur C. Clarke,

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:59.930
author of 2001 and inventor of the communications satellite.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:04.980
Now in retreat in Sri Lanka, after a lifetime of science, space, and writing,

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:07.700
he ponders the riddles of this and other worlds.

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:13.050
I'm standing in front of my bungalow on the extreme southern tip of Sri Lanka.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:17.940
Just over a hundred years ago, according to the London Times,

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:20.930
which is not prone to sensational reporting,

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:27.070
a schooner, the Pearl, of 150 tons, sailed from Gaul Harbour,

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:29.840
which is the next bay to here.

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:40.290
That schooner sailed past here into the Bay of Bengal, and there she was attacked and sunk by a giant squid.

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:46.460
This was observed from a P&O liner, which rescued some of the survivors from the schooner.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:54.130
It's an incredible story, but when one considers the enormous amount of unexplored ocean,

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:59.820
there are 6,000 miles of empty sea from here to the icy walls of Antarctica.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:08.190
One can believe that out there lurked unknown and perhaps gigantic monsters still unknown to science.

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:43.510
The late Lieutenant R.E. Grimani Cox was returning home to England in 1942

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:48.060
when he encountered one of the Second World War's most nightmarish sea stories.

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:54.060
His troop ship was sunk by a German raider in the South Atlantic.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:59.440
Cox found himself on a fragile raft beset by sharks.

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:02.770
After five days came a sinister assault.

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:06.480
Cox showed the evidence later to a friend.

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:11.000
When I looked at his leg, he pulled up his trousers

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:13.640
and I could see scars the size of a penny,

00:03:13.820 --> 00:03:16.720
which is about an inch and a quarter of the old penny,

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:20.020
were dotted at intervals all the way up his leg.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:23.900
These were white scars sunk quite deep into the flesh

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:25.680
where the skin had been pulled off.

00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:29.980
Before he died in 1971, Cox told...

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:35.100
the story to his sisters, as well as to his friend, a biologist, Professor Cloudsley-Thompson.

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:42.480
Yes, he didn't show me that. He only showed me that. Well, you were his sisters, and this

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:49.910
was in the mess. There were 12 of them on the raft initially, and only three survived

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:55.230
to the end of the five days. And one of the most horrifying things that happened while

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:58.850
while they were lying there dying one by one from thirst.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:05.910
was one evening when they were attacked by a giant squid.

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:09.190
An enormous shape appeared beside the raft,

00:04:09.230 --> 00:04:13.180
and a huge arm came over and snatched one of the men

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:16.240
and tore him off the raft before anybody could do anything to save him.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:18.540
And presumably he was eaten.

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:22.210
And they were still barely recovering from the shock of this

00:04:22.210 --> 00:04:25.760
when another arm or tentacle came over the side of the raft.

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:28.040
He saw it slurred against the...

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:29.220
The, the, the, the...

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:36.040
starlit sky and it fastened itself on him around his leg and around his body particularly his right

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:40.420
leg because that's where the scars mainly were he showed me but I believe he said that they were on

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:45.900
the rest of his body as well and he'd have been pulled off just like the others only fortunately

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:51.090
by that time people were alert and so they grabbed on and held him and instead of him being pulled

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:55.870
over the side the suckers pulled lumps of skin off him off his body and this is what caused these

00:04:55.870 --> 00:04:58.590
a massive number of scars all over him.

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:11.520
On her maiden voyage out of San Diego, the U.S. Navy frigate Stein also had a weird encounter.

